\midiclock enables or disables MIDI clock messages sent
by the sequencer of LiveLily.
Its syntax is the following:

\midiclock on

Its arguments are either on or off.

The MIDI clock is sent to the ports opened with
\openmidiport, so open one first, otherwise \midiclock on
gives an error and the clock stays off:

\listmidiports
\openmidiport 1
\midiclock on

With more ports opened with \openmidiport, the clock is
sent to all of them. The ports that only instruments have
opened (with their midiport method) don't get it.
